18034526463576"}]}, "baseline_offer": {"id": "1318034526463576"}, "is_approved": true, "firstOffer": {"nodes": [{"start_time": 1781216040, "status": "PUBLISHED", "id": "1318034526463576"}]}, "liveChannel": {"nodes": [{"latest_supported_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "id": "1138886909315908", "version": "2.4"}, "id": "36981254941459587", "channel_name": "LIVE"}]}, "is_for_oculus_keys_only": false, "primary_binaries": {"nodes": [{"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1092172207320712", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1138886909315908"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "36981254941459587"}]}, "change_log": "Online Stargazing Events (LIVE Feature) Added\r\n\r\nDeep Sky Finder now lets you host online stargazing events from your own observing location.\r\n\r\nAs a host, you can share a sky map based on your current observing location with participants and introduce your own images of deep-sky objects such as nebulae, star clusters, and galaxies. Registered images can be displayed at the positions of their corresponding Messier objects in the sky.\r\n\r\nParticipants can join an active event by selecting it from the LIVE list. Once joined, they can view the sky based on the host\u2019s observing location rather than their own current location, directly in Quest.\r\n\r\nYou can share your favorite astrophotography images with astronomy friends in distant locations.\r\n\r\nMain New Features\r\nAdded the ability to host and join LIVE stargazing events\r\nSelect an active event from the LIVE event list\r\nShare the sky based on the host\u2019s observing location with participants\r\nDisplay registered images on participants\u2019 Quest screens\r\nAdded the ability for participants to send \u201cGood!\u201d reactions to the host\r\n\r\nEnjoy a new kind of online stargazing event using your own night sky and the images of the universe that you have captured.", "created_date": 1783384200, "id": "1138886909315908", "version": "2.4", "version_code": 5, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1092172207320712", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1138886909315908"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "36981254941459587"}]}, "change_log": "Deep Sky Finder V2.3\r\n\r\nThis update adds three new features to make exploring the night sky more visual and intuitive.\r\n\r\nMoon Phase Display\r\nThe Moon is now shown with its current phase. The illuminated side rotates toward the Sun\u2019s direction, helping you understand the appearance of the Moon from a thin crescent to a full Moon.\r\n\r\nDisplay Images for All Messier Objects\r\nYou can now display small image thumbnails for all Messier objects. This makes it easier to see the locations and appearances of nebulae, star clusters, and galaxies directly in the sky. \r\n\r\nReplace Messier Object Images\r\nLong-press a Messier object to replace its displayed image with your own. Select a JPG or PNG image saved in the Quest Downloads folder and customize the sky with your preferred astrophotography images.", "created_date": 1781920458, "id": "1112065568664709", "version": "2.3", "version_code": 4, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBina